{
  "id": "ticket_01KZ28482RCAKQPKTXJQ82FJW1",
  "name": "Make the test suite safe for concurrent runs on one machine",
  "slug": "make-the-test-suite-safe",
  "spec": {
    "summary": "Multiple agents running the suite concurrently produce flaky failures (spawnSync status null on slop init and friends). Root-cause with evidence, then fix so N concurrent full-gate runs in separate worktrees are reliably green. Prefer injected/mocked seams over incidental system-level dependencies; keep the real-binary acceptance philosophy where it is load-bearing.",
    "details_md": "Observed incidents: (1) 15 spawn-flakes (spawnSync status null on slop init) when suite accidentally ran 3x concurrently; (2) 43 phantom failures from a stale shared dist/slop when running in the main checkout; (3) general guidance since then has been to serialize all agent gates, which slows every multi-agent workflow. Suspects: process/memory storms from vitest-workers x spawned 96MB binaries (spawnSync null = kill or EAGAIN/ENOMEM - capture the actual errno), port collisions in web/Playwright fixtures, shared build artifacts (dist/slop, src/web/generated) as implicit mutable state.",
    "acceptance": [
      "Documented, evidence-backed root cause for each failure mode (actual errno/signal captured, not guessed)",
      "3 concurrent full-suite runs in separate worktrees pass repeatedly; a reproduction/regression script proves it"
    ],
